Z||000023||Patrick's Dad||08-15-2001||09:18 PM||||&lt;quote&gt;So I guess you dont like get 'stem'ulated by stem cell research? Anyone remember..<BR>                       "The good of the many outweigh(s) the good of the few or the one"? sacrificing one 'unborn human' is not worth helping other born humans?&lt;/quote&gt;<P>Galen, Mr. Spock &lt;i&gt;chose&lt;/i&gt; to give his life for the many, and his Katra was in Dr. McCoy anyway.<P>Why don't we just take a random human being, with out their consent, and tear their limbs off (D&C abortion), or burn them to death (saline), or poke a hole in the back of their necks and suck out the contents of their skull (PBA). After all, more food, more air, and more money for the rest of us....<P>This ought to get me a stern warning from Cliff....<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick's Dad (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||EdsB52||08-16-2001||03:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fogglethorpe:<BR>[B]B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"1) I must sacrifice some degree of personal liberty to be safe. (Or, I will be safer without a gun)"<BR>-If that's a liberal fallacy, them why did one of our most conservative Presidents of all time have his NRA card revoked?<P>"2)Keeping more of my money makes me greedy, and hurts the economy. In fact, it is my civic duty to have 40% of my income confiscated."<BR>-George Bush Sr signed the largest tax increase in history. Please, no liberal Congress rationale; he signed it fair and square.<P>"3)SUV's are the worst invention of all time, are driven by evil, cigar chomping  capitalists, and will eventually cause an environmental meltdown, which will end the world."<BR>-Please, couldn't you refer to Lear jets or something more substantial than a mini-bus? I don't believe SUV's are the even on the list of priorities for the liberal left.<P>"4)The so-called news media is the 4th branch of government."<BR>-The right b!tch about the media as much as do the left. The right says they’re too liberal, the left says they're an arm of the government.<P>"5)All speech is protected by the United States Constitution, unless it's "hate speech" (i.e., religious or politically conservative)."<BR>-Are you carefully saying the liberals don't revere religious speech as worthy of protection? If so, not true. The left just wants a degree of sanctuary, in that freedom of speech also means freedom from speech. To mandate certain speech is an infringement to the concept of 'freedom of speech.'<P>"6)Morality is not black and white, but is defined by individual choice. (Or, feelings are mightier than truth)"<BR>-So you're saying that morality is black and white. Ok, should homosexuals be allowed to cohabitate? Should a woman have the right to abort her fetus during the first term? How about in the occurrence of rape? How about incest? Should opposite sex heterosexuals be allowed to cohabitate in a sexual relationship? Should a person have the right to peacefully, painlessly euthanize themselves? Certain elements of life are black and white as far as ethical behavior goes, like murder, rape, robbery, etc.  These forms of behavior are unethical or heinous (immoral) prima facie. But other forms of behavior that include mutual voluntaryness are very gray. What do you feel the difference between amoral and immoral is? And how does it affect this topic? Please, answer ALL the above questions, not just the easier ones while omitting the more gray ones. Feel free to give an explanation after your answer. <P>"7)All life is precious, especially that of suckerfish, spotted owls, and various unnamed foliage in the rain forests. Unborn human babies, however, are unviable tissue masses, and therefore unworthy of protection under the law (unless they are harvested for medical research)."<BR>-All life is precious is a liberal concept? I thought that was a human concept. Or is it that conservatives are inhumane?<P>"8)The United States has the worst healthcare system in the entire known universe, and must instead revert to a socialized system which has failed miserably everywhere else it's been tried."<BR>-What is your option, HMO's? The difference between HMO's and socialized medicine, similar to that of Canada, is that unemployed and homeless people lose their right for access to health care (other than emergencies). Another distinction is that with socialized medicine, the federal government is responsible to decide the level of care that is going to be universally dispersed. With HMO's, the government leaves it up to corporations to decide who lives or dies. Then with Bush placing ceilings on damage awards against HMO's, if it becomes cheaper to pay the maximum damage award than to operate over the long run, the corporation might make the their best business decision.<P>"9)The Federal Government is the provider, protector, and empowerer of all people."<BR>-It's amazing at how many people that work for the government, or one of its contractors, will echo this sentiment (the conservative version).<P>"10)Rich people are vermin, and acquired their wealth on the backs of the poor. For this, they should be severely punished by litigation and taxation."<BR>-One out of 10 aint bad!!!<P>Yes, you shall go on. But first please answer all of my points, not just the less painful ones. Nice perspectives though; I look forward to a fun exchange with you, Ed.||||reg||1
Z||000025||EdsB52||08-16-2001||03:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>To quote Julie Winters,<BR>"A Liberal is a Conservative who hasn't been mugged."<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A libertarian is a disgruntled conservative. So look, the parties aren't opposed as popular consensus would yield, they're aligned on a continuum.||||reg||1
Z||000026||EdsB52||08-16-2001||03:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>If I agree with the SUV statement, does that make me a liberal?  I'm pretty conservative, otherwise.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, it proves that other than Jerry Falwell and Rush Limbaugh that people are generally bipartisan. Few people have beliefs that are at the extreme bookends of the continuum.||||reg||1
Z||000027||EdsB52||08-16-2001||03:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Ok, I need to add one more.<BR>Election results should be recounted as many times as it takes, until the liberals (democrats) win.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How many dirty elections should the conservatives be allowed to have before disqualification? Nixon only had one (that we know of), but Bush is on his second one. I find it so ironic for the Republican Party to call the Democrats cheaters in this election. We all know the forte of the democrats is too get as much tail as possible while in office [Kennedy(s)and Clinton], whereas the Republicans want to cheat at elections whenever possible (Nixon and Bush). ||||reg||1
Z||000028||EdsB52||08-16-2001||04:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B><BR>And we're getting very close to that.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Get real. The definition of rich is anyone who makes more money than YOU DO!  If you make $20K a year, you don't want to pay taxes, but tax that rich bastard who makes $40K a year."<P>That might work at a local level, such as your next-door neighbor or the guy down the block. But if we look at it macrostructurally, we can examine the class levels and the ability/inability to have mobility between these levels. We might realize how right Ray really is when we examine the entirety of the class structure, not just one specific rung.<P>"I'm paying about 40% in taxes (everything combined), and I'm no where near rich.  Do you see me complaining about people who make more than I do?  No."<P>If you look at it more like distribution of this countries wealth, you'll gain a different perspective. If they tax the lower classes at a rate that disallows them investment or expendable income, they're subjugating or at least oppressing the lower classes through distribution of wealth.<P>"I don't like paying that much in taxes, and when I can make a change by voting, I do it."<P>Don't fool yourself! Bush signed the largest tax increase in history as well he had his NRA card yanked. What do you think of the party specific fallacies now?<P>"Remember, it's not government's job to provide for the people.  That would be socialism."<P>Actually you have socialism confused for communism. The American Heritage Dictionary (2,000 pager) defines communism as: "A system of government in which the state plans and controls the economy and a single, often authoritarian party holds power, claiming to make progress toward a higher social order in which all goods are equally shared by the people." <BR>The same dictionary defines socialism as: "A social system in which the means of producing and distributing goods are owned collectively and political power is exercised by the whole community."<P>The above two forms of social/economic systems are often confused for each other. The political/moral right (as well as the rich) does what they can to proliferate and disseminate this disinformation to create fear and anxiety so they can maintain control over the proletariat. In my opinion the cold war had many objectives, and this was one of them. In fact, in the depression era many Americans almost turned to communism, so even the rich helped vote out Hoover. The point there is that the rich and conservative want proletariats to hang in the lower-middle; subscribe to capitalism, but stay just well-off enough not to be curious and explore socialism. What do you think a barter system is? It's socialism. Read the above definition and refute me. How many flag-waving conservatives are for a barter system? Me too and I’m not one. This post might anger some, but please, it's intent is designed to educate and constructively argue. So by all means, refute my assertions.<P>Oh, by the way, Canadian socialism or Scandinavian socialism are the best forms of government in the world IMHO.||||reg||1
Z||000029||EdsB52||08-16-2001||04:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR>[B][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Democrats are always saying we should "pay our fair share".  Well how much is that?"<P>Too dynamic to answer in one post.<P>"Ans.:  Well, we don't know but no matter how much you are paying, it should be more."<P>Oh, you must be one of the wealthy 2%, lucky guy.<P>"The answer isn't tax increases or cuts, its SPENDING cuts.  Quit spending on programs that have never worked and never will work."<P>Oh, like the B-1B? I worked on the B-52 in the AF and the B-1B in manufacturing. You don't need to be an expert on this subject, as I am to understand that the B-1B is a waste and the military is afraid to use it in war. Carter cut it; Reagan reinstated it. Again, incompetence isn't left or right, it's across the board.<P>"Remember several years ago when they refused to pass a budget so the government "shut down" for a while?  How many of you even noticed or cared?  That should tell you something."<P>What should it have told us? Please, finish your thought. I feel like I have to disclaim every time I post. Please do not take this as an attack, just respond.||||reg||1
Z||000030||EdsB52||08-16-2001||04:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR>[B][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Let's keep it friendly. <P>"They confirmed once and for all that George Bush DID win the majority down there - no question."<P>Did they address the contention that the polls closed early in the poor areas?<P>"Mr. Clinton and his buddies haven't done anything for you in 8 years."<P>I realize the economy’s condition can't be fully credited/blamed on the administration, but the economy did enjoy the most prosperous time ever. Clinton helped make it possible for me to afford and attend college. Clinton helped knock down many ceilings and barriers for the less advantaged. <P>"It looks like your country is finally heading in the righ direction."<P>Bush killed the Ergonomics Bill that OSHA started. Nixon started OSHA in the early 70's. Bush is trying to make it impossible for lower/lower-middle class people to file bankruptcy. Bush redistributed the national surplus for popularity value, instead of paying off the debt. Bush took the ABA out of the process of researching federal judges, providing less checks-and-balances. Bush is working toward limits on HMO damage awards. This is all I can think of for now, but are these examples of what you're referring? Easy to say from up there.<P>“It appears that you have let yourself be swayed by the Liberal (Democratic) media that has been bad-mouthing your president from the get-go.”<P>Shouldn’t they be able to?||||reg||1
Z||000031||Galen||08-16-2001||06:50 AM||||Ed, I know you've been told this before. and I rightfully dont care what you have to say in response.. but you talk too much. and sound too .. well.. its a big word that my 'republican' mind can't proccess<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"With one drop of blood he realized his own mortallity, it was then he saw the true face of God. For he is not someone watching down on us, but he is in us." - Galen 2001</FONT>||||reg||1
